.TH FATHOM_NOTE_ADD 1  "fathom 0.1.0-alpha.1" 
.SH NAME
fathom\-note\-add \- Record a note, decision, question or follow\-up against an episode or a path
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBfathom note add\fR [\fB\-\-episode\fR] [\fB\-\-path\fR] [\fB\-\-kind\fR] [\fB\-\-author\fR] [\fB\-\-agent\fR] [\fB\-\-about\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fITEXT\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Record a note, decision, question or follow\-up against an episode or a path
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-episode\fR \fI<EPISODE>\fR
The episode to attach it to, or an unambiguous prefix of its id
.TP
\fB\-\-path\fR \fI<PATH>\fR
The path to attach it to, optionally `path:line`. Resolved to the newest episode that touched it when the index knows one
.TP
\fB\-\-kind\fR \fI<KIND>\fR [default: annotation]
What kind of note this is: `decision`, `question`, `follow\-up`, `annotation` (`note` and `flag` are accepted as `annotation`)
.TP
\fB\-\-author\fR \fI<AUTHOR>\fR
Who is writing, when git config and `fathom.toml` do not say
.TP
\fB\-\-agent\fR \fI<AGENT>\fR
Record the note as an agent\*(Aqs act on someone\*(Aqs behalf, not as a human\*(Aqs
.TP
\fB\-\-about\fR \fI<ABOUT>\fR
The note this one answers, by `nt\-…` id
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
[\fITEXT\fR]
The text of the note. One line in the file either way: paragraph breaks are folded, never wrapped
